@0    = ~Sahuagin attacked this city. They took a sacred artifact from our Queen's Temple! You defeated the rearguard of the defiling creatures. You are chosen to pursue them and retrieve the stolen relic!~
@1    = ~Excuse me?~
@2    = ~I'm listening.~
@3    = ~I don't think you have the authority to "choose" me for anything.~
@4    = ~Nice that you decided to join *now*!~
@5    = ~Silence! You will listen.~
@6    = ~The sahuagin came through a portal in the underground pond. This was not a Wild Hunt, but a targeted attack. They were aiming for the temple of our queen, temple of this city. It was an attack on Baldur's Gate!~
@7    = ~I'm still not sure what I have to do with this.~
@8    = ~Go on.~
@9    = ~A sahuagin attack on the city would be bad. Why tell me all this, though? You should speak to the authorities.~
@10   = ~Lady, maybe you should evaluate your recruiting standards. I had a hostile confrontation in your temple, and now you want me as a mercenary?~
@11   = ~Why do you ask me of all people?~
@12   = ~Do I look like I care?~
@13   = ~Pfeh, "authorities". The temple of our Queen is the only authority I answer to!~
@14   = ~Here, you were in the right place at the right time. You defeated the trespassing creatures. You are as well suited as any.~
@15   = ~The sahuagin defiled our holy relic, Iakhovas' Tooth. This is an extremely sacred artifact that has been with us longer than the city has borne its current name. It found its way to us through the city's founder, Balduran, who gave it to us as a token to gain the Queen's favor for his sea voyages. With the tooth gone, what do you think Umberlee's favor for the city will look like?~
@16   = ~Not good, I wager. Fine, you have my interest. What now?~
@17   = ~You are seriously putting the whole city's fate's blame onto me, aren't you?~
@18   = ~A tooth? Surely this is a jest?~
@19   = ~Maybe it will look like the fate that will meet you now, for pestering me with such details. I have no interest in pursuing your 'holy tooth'. How about we have a look whether your teeth all sit tight, huh?~
@20   = ~Do not ridicule what is sacred! The Tooth stands for Umberlee's Power and Wrath for those who disappoint and hurt our Queen. It is a sign of what will happen to those who defile our Lady's name!~
@21   = ~Fine, you have my interest. What now?~
@22   = ~And that got stolen. Hahaha, now it is a sign for your 'power' even more—you are, literally, *toothless* and want to rely on the first armed person walking by to retrieve it.~
@23   = ~Do not question your usefulness for Umberlee's intent! But I *will* shut your mouth if you continue to be so disrespectful.~
@24   = ~Lady, you want me to help, so watch your tone!~
@25   = ~You will follow the portal and retrieve the Sacred Tooth!~
@26   = ~Fine, I'll do it.~
@27   = ~I might, but not right now!~
@28   = ~What will be my reward?~
@29   = ~No, I won't. Try to stop me from not doing it!~
@30   = ~I will close the original portal and open one that leads nearby to where the creatures took our sacred relic.~
@31   = ~Your reward will be all treasures you'll find amongst the sahuagin! Keep anything you want, but bring the tooth to us!~
@32   = ~In other words, you don't have a reward for me. *sigh* Fine, I'll do it.~
@33   = ~It is done. You are free to enter. Retrieve the tooth, and the portal will lead you back here. Don't delay your departure too long—our Queen is impatient, and it will only make your task more difficult. And... do not seek support for this task in the temple, nor speak to anyone about this, or the wrath of my goddess will smash you!~ [bsblank]
@34   = ~What are you waiting for? Follow the portal and do what our Queen expects of you!~
@35   = ~Tell me where the portal will take me, first!~
@36   = ~Why aren't you going yourself? Surely the temple has the necessary resources to fight some sahuagin.~
@37   = ~Your queen, not mine.~
@38   = ~You *are* aware that I killed priestesses in your temple, yes? But you are recruiting me anyhow for such a sensible mission?~
@39   = ~Er, portal... where exactly?~
@40   = ~I changed my mind. I couldn't care less about your tooth. I will not get it back.~
@41   = ~Farewell.~
@42   = ~What did you not understand when I said "portal in the underground pond"? It's here, right before your eyes. You'll have to dive to get to it.~
@43   = ~You will be at her mercy, so you better show respect!~
@44   = ~I do not have to reveal my reasons to you!~
@45   = ~You want me to go through an unknown portal and fight sea creatures for you. Why can't you go yourself? Is there some kind of conflict of interest with regard to Umberlee's children?~
@46   = ~Are you afraid to go yourself?~
@47   = ~Whatever. Farewell.~
@48   = ~The sahuagin started the confrontation by taking our Sacred Tooth!~
@49   = ~So there *is* some kind of restriction for you to go after them. Why would it be safe for me, then? I don't wish to attract Umberlee's wrath any more than you!~
@50   = ~Do you think my Queen is so petty as not to see who is sending you?~
@51   = ~I am not afraid! You are mercenaries, hired to do the Queen's bidding. Do not annoy me any more!~
@52   = ~Bring back the Tooth, and Umberlee will not be displeased with your services.~
@53   = ~How does it help you to know which secluded island it is? Fine, if you *must* know, it's a small island in the Moonshae Seas.~
@54   = ~You *are* aware that I killed the High Priestess in your temple, yes? But you are recruiting me anyhow for such a sensible mission?~
@55   = ~The Queen is granting you a chance to redeem yourself. Retrieving the Tooth is of utmost importance.~
@56   = ~You imbeciles! Feel the wrath of the Bitch Queen!~
@57   = ~We were too patient with you! Feel the wrath of the Bitch Queen!~
@58   = ~Here they are!~
@59   = ~You killed our sister, so you forfeit your right to live. I will take the sacred tooth after killing you.~
@60   = ~You return victorious! Hand over the relic and fulfill our Queen's intent!~
@61   = ~Well, retrieving the tooth is why I went, so here you have it.~
@62   = ~You lied to me! The tooth was *given* to the sahuagin as a token of joined forces and a mutual agreement to have the sahuagin attack Baldur's Gate!~
@63   = ~You sent other adventurers after the tooth before! The sahuagin in the sea cave weren't part of the group that actually took the tooth!~
@64   = ~To what place did you send me? Umberlee's wrath hit people venturing into that temple!~
@65   = ~Whoops, seems I misplaced it.~
@66   = ~No need for more words. I decided not to give you the tooth, so I guess this means we fight.~
@67   = ~You've made a wise choice.~
@68   = ~I do not want any trouble with the Water Queen, so farewell.~
@69   = ~I have no proof for your betrayal other than my statement, so you'll come with me and confess to the city authorities.~
@70   = ~Not so fast. You sent other adventurers after the tooth before! The sahuagin in the sea cave weren't part of the group that actually took the tooth!~
@71   = ~How can you be so foolish as to approach us without the sacred relic?~
@72   = ~I'll go and get it.~
@73   = ~*tch* And can you prove that bold claim?~
@74   = ~I have no proof for your betrayal yet, but while I'm holding onto the tooth, you can go and confess to the city authorities.~
@75   = ~I don't have the tooth with me.~
@76   = ~Of course we did not only send one group of adventurers. Do you believe us fools?~
@77   = ~Were you scared? And yet here you are, back in one piece, so until now, you seem to have done everything right.~
@78   = ~My patience is running out. You brought back The Tooth of Iakhovas—we will retrieve it!~
@79   = ~We will do no such thing!~
@80   = ~A-hahaha! You really thought that would've worked?~
@81   = ~Sisters, our work here is done. This vermin is not worth our efforts.~
@82   = ~The Sacred Tooth is ours again! You were an obedient servant, so I will spare your life.~
@83   = ~You have brought the vengeance of the Water Queen upon yourself!~
@84   = ~(The creature says something heated in the sahuagin tongue of whistles, clicks and snarls. It is obvious that it is hostile.)~
@85   = ~You desecrated the portal rooms!~
@86   = ~You destroyed the portals. Do you think that saved you, soft land dwellers, from what we planned? You fool, all you gained is more time. We will come with many—and your city will be the first to fall!~
@87   = ~You saw something you were not supposed to see. You earned your land dwellers more time by killing our architect. We respect your strength, so you will walk out alive. Do not touch anything else, or we will destroy you like the vermin you are.~
@88   = ~You have what you came for. There is no need for you to tarry on this island.~
@89   = ~Decide which faction you want to support, and do it quickly! My patience is running out.~
@90   = ~(The creature is obviously arguing with another sahuagin. It says something in the sahuagin language, not addressed at you.)~
@91   = ~You are done here. Leave.~
@92   = ~Any chance we could still get temple services?~
@93   = ~I'll be gone soon.~
@94   = ~(The creature says something heated in the sahuagin tongue of whistles, clicks and snarls to the sahuagin priestess.)~
@95   = ~(The creature replies shortly to the first sahuagin, then turning its attention to you.)~
@96   = ~I have called on Sekolah to give these beings the ability to understand our tongue. They are intelligent land creatures of the kinds we already know, but these look different from those hiding in the corridors. They seem to be well-armed and an opponent worth considering.~
@97   = ~Then they will understand if I tell them that I will gain honor by slaying them in Sekolah's name!~
@98   = ~Don't make a fool of yourself, Frohxlto. Our dispute must have made it obvious to you that you'll need allies for what you have in mind. Attacking a baron who is carrying out King Ixilthetocal's sacred orders will bring you nothing but your own death, so weigh wisely the opportunities presented by the appearance of these beings.~
@99   = ~You—come talk to me when Baron Frohxlto is done with you. If neither of you is so primitive as to start a fight on this first meeting, of course.~
@100  = ~You, land creature. Priestess Ilxigantl said you could be of use to me. Why are you here?~
@101  = ~I am here to retrieve a relic, a tooth of sorts. Your people took it from a Temple of Umberlee.~
@102  = ~No need for much talk. I guess I rather just kill you.~
@103  = ~The Taker's Tooth it is you are after? Ghrumshrtl has it. His followers call it the tooth of the One Who Swims With Sekolah and believe it to hold power and the favor of Umberlee. Ever since he came back with it, he and his followers behave like they are Sekolah's Chosen.~
@104  = ~It seems we have the same goal, land creature. Baron Ghrumshrtl lost the way, I need him dead so I can take his place. Priestess Ilxigantl is right that I can't kill him myself without annoying the king. Kill Ghrumshrtl for me and you can leave this place with the tooth.~
@105  = ~I'll take the deal. I'll kill the other baron for you.~
@106  = ~Wait, so basically, I need to confront the other baron for the tooth anyhow because he probably won't give it to me voluntarily, and you will not attack and let me leave with the tooth if I kill the baron? You have a deal!~
@107  = ~What if I decline?~
@108  = ~Then your own value will be that of a hunt trophy by which I can impress Ghrumshrtl's followers and show that I am the better leader.~
@109  = ~Shall we fight?~
@110  = ~I'll take the deal. I'll kill the other Baron for you.~
@111  = ~You were hunting the castaways, even took a child! I will kill you where you stand!~
@112  = ~Stop talking and draw your weapons!~
@113  = ~I'll watch your steps, landling. Do not try to play me for a fool.~
@114  = ~You did it. Our deal stands.~
@115  = ~Leave this place from where you came, I will not tarry time with you further.~
@116  = ~I know you met with Ghrumshrtl. Why is he still alive?~
@117  = ~I am waiting for you to fulfill your deal! Do not tarry too long, I need to take over reign before the king loses patience with our tarry.~
@118  = ~Not so impatient. I'm working on it.~
@119  = ~The deal is off. The other baron had a better one. Draw your weapons!~
@120  = ~I decided I'll kill you anyhow.~
@121  = ~*snarl*~
@122  = ~I don't need weapons to kill you, soft landling.~
@123  = ~Here you are. Let us talk.~
@124  = ~You still have unfinished business with Baron Frohxlto. Do you think you can outrun him and confront Ghrumshrtl?~
@125  = ~We'll see. Why did you want to talk to me?~
@126  = ~I definitely think I can deal with him and take you out, too. Fight!~
@127  = ~You killed Baron Frohxlto.~
@128  = ~Baron Frohxlto was wise enough to hire you to confront Baron Ghrumshrtl for him.~
@129  = ~It might seem contradictory to you, but my main goal is peace amongst the workers here. We have a greater goal to accomplish. I do not care under whose surveillance it will be finished, but this ridiculous quarrel between the two barons needs to stop, one way or the other.~
@130  = ~If Baron Frohxlto were to attack and kill Baron Ghrumshrtl with his own claws, he will be punished himself, and I will have to take responsibility for both of them stepping out of line. The same applies to Baron Ghrumshrtl, of course, and so the two barons are currently locked in a standoff, trying to impress the other's supporters and lure them in to gain the upper hand.~
@131  = ~Baron Ghrumshrtl on the other hand got distracted from why we are here, too. He started a silly Wild Hunt operation upon your land creature's abode to please his followers. I assume this is the reason you are here. I *told* him it would lead to complications, but he wouldn't stop, arguing that he conspired with land creatures themselves, increasing the gained treasures and food that will be to our advantage. The presence of you land creatures gives credence to my doubts that such an organized Wild Hunt would not have its own repercussions.~
@132  = ~Of course I'd wish they would all end their foolish behavior and work on our task with full capacity, but I lost hope they'll come to their senses. If bringing peace to this site means one party has to be eliminated, so be it. You would be the tool to make it possible without bringing the king's wrath upon all of us.~
@133  = ~Or is eliminating us all your goal?~
@134  = ~I took a deal with the rebel Baron since it seems I have to kill the other Baron anyhow to get what I came for.~
@135  = ~Baron Ghrumshrtl started using the portals for raids at the coast. While a certain number of treasure hunts are acceptable, he has now exaggerated the scope and scale to such an extent that our actual work is suffering as a result.~
@136  = ~As to the conspiracy he mentioned, this is a question you best pose Baron Ghrumshrtl himself.~
@137  = ~What do you mean, it attracts land dwellers? Were there more who came for the tooth?~
@138  = ~What are you sahuagin doing here?~
@139  = ~I have no more questions for you. What now?~
@140  = ~I've decided to kill you. Fight!~
@141  = ~You are not the first, but you seem to be the most powerful.~
@142  = ~Nothing we can't handle, but it is getting tedious. At this rate, it will attract the king's attention.~
@143  = ~Wild Hunt, but in cooperation with people from Baldur's Gate? What do you mean?~
@144  = ~We are making this abandoned place a holy temple, a sacred enclave. Sekolah will smile upon us favorably. It is of no concern to you, land creature.~
@145  = ~So you are one of those who came to retrieve the Tooth of Iakhovas. I see. Baron Ghrumshrtl and his followers see it as an endorsement for our goal in this place, while Baron Frohxlto despises the idea simply because Ghrumshrtl values it. I myself am willing to part with it. It attracts too many land dwellers, and if its return ensures restored peace between us, even better.~
@146  = ~What did you come here for?~
@147  = ~So you agreed to kill Baron Ghrumshrtl, and Baron Frohxlto will leave you the tooth for it. I see. Yes, it is surely one way this could go. I have another suggestion.~
@148  = ~I have a suggestion.~
@149  = ~I will go and convince Baron Ghrumshrtl that he needs to stop his Wild Hunts before it provokes our king's anger. I will make it clear to him that otherwise, appearances of land dwellers will only increase, which *will* endanger our mission. I will make him give you the tooth as a sign that he has really come to his senses.~
@150  = ~I do not expect Baron Ghrumshrtl to give in without any compensation. He will most likely expect you to kill Baron Frohxlto for him in return.~
@151  = ~You already killed the rebels for him—this will be your leverage for these negotiations. There doesn't need to be more bloodshed.~
@152  = ~Why would you do that?~
@153  = ~Fine, I'll talk to your baron.~
@154  = ~I see you decided to kill Baron Ghrumshrtl. Very well, so be it. It might seem contradictory to you, but my main goal is peace amongst the workers here. We have a greater goal to accomplish. Baron Frohxlto is our baron now. I will go down into the quarters. Collect whatever reward you were promised and leave this place.~
@155  = ~So be it. Baron Ghrumshrtl is on the level below. I will be in one of the quarters downstairs, in case you are in need of the Shark Lord's services. As long as you are working for one of the barons, I would be willing to ensure that your physical condition allows it.~
@156  = ~Make a choice.~
@157  = ~Like I said, I want the workers to return to their obligations, and as fast as possible.~
@158  = ~Keeping the current leader will stir as little commotion as possible, so it is to be preferred.~
@159  = ~But Baron Ghrumshrtl needs to let go of his silly side endeavors. You will be the tool whose mere presence will help me to bring him back under control.~
@160  = ~Your choice is unwise, land creature, but so be it.~
@161  = ~Do you need the Shark Father's services?~
@162  = ~Yes, show me what you've got.~
@163  = ~Not now.~
@164  = ~You must be the land creatures Priestess Ilxigantl talked about. The priestess granted you Sekolah's blessing to understand our tongue, so I will listen. Repeat to me why you are here.~
@165  = ~I came here for the tooth from the Temple of Umberlee.~
@166  = ~A question first. Is it true that you were given the tooth relic? I was sent here to retrieve it on the assumption that it had been stolen.~
@167  = ~How about we just fight?~
@168  = ~I won't make deals with creatures that see us as food!~
@169  = ~I agreed to kill you for the other baron, no need to talk any more.~
@170  = ~I would love to fight you, intruders to our realm. But our priestess took great pains to ensure that we talk. So—talk!~
@171  = ~I came here for the tooth you took from the Temple of Umberlee.~
@172  = ~No, we fight.~
@173  = ~Insidious land creatures! So Priestess Ilxigantl told the truth that you are here to take it back. Who sent you?~
@174  = ~Why are you calling me insidious? I was told you stole the tooth from the temple.~
@175  = ~The Temple of Umberlee.~
@176  = ~A priestess of Umberlee.~
@177  = ~What does it matter? You stole it, I will return it.~
@178  = ~What does it matter?~
@179  = ~I am no thief! You mean because I take from you land creatures my treasures and trophies? The tooth is not one of those.~
@180  = ~The temple, you say. So, first they talk about agreements, then they send mercenaries?~
@181  = ~One priestess, you say. Does she not speak for her temple? First they talk about agreements, then they send mercenaries!~
@182  = ~The Tooth of The One Who Swims With Sekolah is a pledge to our agreement. We hunt in the city of underground rivers, and the temple does not interfere! It is you who is trespassing for wanting it back!~
@183  = ~Wait—are you implying that the Temple of Umberlee made an arrangement with you to go on raids inside Baldur's Gate?~
@184  = ~I don't believe you. You are trying to manipulate me into abandoning my mission!~
@185  = ~It is of no importance any more. Priestess Ilxigantl showed wisdom with her warnings that land creatures will come and endanger our mission. I wanted to give my people potential for enjoyment and for more valuables and food to boost our work here, but your interference opened my eyes. I need neither the Tooth of The One Who Swims With Sekolah nor an agreement with Umberlee's priestesses to achieve that.~
@186  = ~I could kill you and be done with it, but Priestess Ilxigantl convinced me that you can be to my advantage, and I agree that the benefit overweighs the loss of the Sacred Tooth. Kill the rebel baron for me, and I will let you leave from this island with the tooth.~
@187  = ~Fine, I will do that for you.~
@188  = ~Well, he is already dead.~
@189  = ~No. I agreed to kill you for the other baron, and I chose to honor this agreement.~
@190  = ~Let me think about it.~
@191  = ~You know what? We talked—now let us fight.~
@192  = ~No, no "thinking about it". We either fight now, or you take my deal!~
@193  = ~Good choice.~
@194  = ~Bring me the baron's head!~
@195  = ~So this is how it will go. We will fight!~
@196  = ~I heard you killed the rebels. I will honor our deal.~
@197  = ~Here is the tooth.~
@198  = ~Give it to the Bitch Queen's priestesses and tell them that our deal is over—and we will not forget the treason. Next time we come into your city of stones, we will come with many, and we will spare no one.~
@199  = ~Leave.~
@200  = ~But the tooth is gone—you stole it! No matter, you did what we agreed to and have your reward.~
@201  = ~Halt! You have no clearance to enter here. Do not walk any further, or we will stop you with force.~
@202  = ~Get away from the doors.~
@203  = ~Talk to Baron Ghrumshrtl, not us.~
@204  = ~Talk to the priestess, not me.~
@205  = ~Intruder!~
@206  = ~I am watching you.~
@207  = ~Talk to Baron Frohxlto, not me.~
@208  = ~Behave yourself.~
@209  = ~Talk to Baron Ghrumshrtl, not me.~
@210  = ~I have a relic of the Temple of Umberlee here and would like to ask you to return it. I retrieved it for them, but there was a... misunderstanding when I tried to hand it in.~
@211  = ~I see. Thank you, my child. Even if churches do not always agree, it is courtesy to respect holy relics. We will see to its safe return.~
@212  = ~[female Talos priestess]I hear you decided against selling the Tooth of Iakhovas to us. You wasted a good opportunity to please the Storm Lord. It is of no use to kill you now. My god will have a better plan for you.~
@213  = ~[female Talos priestess]Greetings, <CHARNAME>. Yes, I know who you are. Let's not dwell on things that might have happened in the recent past. I am Priestess of Talos, and I am approaching you because we know that you hold a relic, sacred to the cursed Temple of the Bitch Queen. We have a vested interest in acquiring this item and are offering you a large sum of gold. Would you be willing to part with it for us?~
@214  = ~You want Iakhovas' Tooth?~
@215  = ~[female Talos priestess]Indeed, that is correct.~
@216  = ~I am listening.~
@217  = ~And why would I give it to you?~
@218  = ~Hand the thing over to the church of the god with whom Umberlee is at odds? Do you think I'm crazy?~
@219  = ~How about I just kill you, instead.~
@220  = ~[female Talos priestess]We will pay you 4,000 gold, in addition to this scroll of Ice Storm for it... and the gratitude of Talos.~
@221  = ~What if I say no?~
@222  = ~Can I think about this?~
@223  = ~No thanks. I'd prefer not to anger Umberlee any more than I already did.~
@224  = ~I'd like to sell you the tooth relic, but I don't have it with me currently.~
@225  = ~Yes, I'd like to please the Storm Lord. Here it is.~
@226  = ~4,000 gold is incredible indeed. Make it at least 5,000, and the relic is yours.~
@227  = ~[female Talos priestess]You might anger Umberlee, but what would it matter if it secures the Storm Lord's favor?~
@228  = ~[female Talos priestess]Then I would attempt to reason with you one more time. Be aware that I will not let go of this opportunity easily.~
@229  = ~[female Talos priestess]What is your decision?~
@230  = ~I said no.~
@231  = ~[female Talos priestess]I suspected asking you nicely would be a mistake. Seems I'll have to take the relic out of your dead hands.~
@232  = ~[female Talos priestess]5,000 it is.~
@233  = ~[female Talos priestess]I believe you know when to play your cards to ensure the favor of the most important and potent god in these realms.~
@234  = ~[female Talos priestess]Come and find me in the Elfsong Tavern if you are willing to sell the tooth relic to me.~
@235  = ~[female Talos priestess]Absolutely not. I believe you know when to play your cards to ensure the favor of the most important and potent god in these realms.~
@236  = ~[female Talos priestess]Greetings, <CHARNAME>. Have you come to a decision regarding the tooth?~
@237  = ~I haven't decided yet.~
@238  = ~[female Talos priestess]Don't wait too long.~
@239  = ~[female Talos priestess]You have seized an excellent opportunity to honor the Storm Lord. Farewell.~
@240  = ~I hear sahuagin stole a relic from your temple. The Priestess of Umberlee who requested I get it back was rather specific about not telling you this, are you even aware?~
@241  = ~I have here the Tooth of Iakhovas, holy relic of your temple.~
@242  = ~I have evidence that some of your priestesses were part of an intrigue against the city.~
@243  = ~You hold our holy tooth—and you killed our sisters for it!~
@244  = ~Hmph. Hand it over at *once* or feel the wrath of the Water Queen!~
@245  = ~Yes, that's why I'm here. Take it, I enjoy a little intrigue here and there, no need to get unfriendly.~
@246  = ~Not so fast. I do believe it should be worth something if I give you this, don't you think? I'm sure the city authorities would be very interested in this, too.~
@247  = ~What, you thought I'd just hand it over to you? I'm just letting you know that I hold something over you, so you'd better remember.~
@248  = ~Iakhovas' Tooth?! If you have received this proof, you must also have acquired our holy relic. Hand it over at once!~
@249  = ~It's only logical I'll give you your relic, too. Here it is.~
@250  = ~I don't have it.~
@251  = ~How about a reward? The relic should be worth something to you, don't you think?~
@252  = ~The Holy Tooth—Takhovas' Tooth—should be with my sisters. If they told you to get it back, what are you waiting for? Retrieve it at once!~
@253  = ~In other words, you had no idea.~
@254  = ~Yes, I will.~
@255  = ~Watch your words. The Bitch Queen brooks no insolence.~
@256  = ~You *dare* speak such words in these halls?~
@257  = ~You *dare* come in here empty handed?~
@258  = ~You made a wise choice today. The Bitch Queen will forgive you your sins—this time. Go now, and don't bother me again.~
@259  = ~Our sisters were killed—and it is you who holds the tooth!~
@260  = ~Well, your sisters were part of a plot ... against your own, as it seems.~
@261  = ~Yes, and if you want it, you should take it quickly, lest I decide otherwise.~
@262  = ~They weren't exactly cooperative. Be glad I'm not taking it out on you.~
@263  = ~Bold statement. Show me the evidence to back your claim!~
@264  = ~This mentions Iakhovas' Tooth. If it belongs together, you must have also acquired our holy relic. Give it to me immediately!~
@265  = ~Whatever you heard or saw, Umberlee will see and hear, too! Her wrath will be boundless against anyone who wronged her. If my sisters requested you bring back our holy relic, what are you waiting for?~
@266  = ~I'm on it.~
@267  = ~You *lost* our holy relic, yet you come in here, thinking you would get out alive?~
@268  = ~It is wise to be obedient to the Water Queen. Go now.~
@269  = ~Leave, now.~
@270  = ~What does it matter to you? Your priestess said you'd have use of me. What do you want?~
@271  = ~It matters to decide whether I should crush you or make use of you. You came here for a reason. State it and it might be your reward if you work for me.~
